30 CM BGL 10.7 M N OF WOODEN FENCE; 18 M W OF W/EDGE OF PARKING LOT 8.1 M NE OF PIPELINE WARNING SIGN</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1370732180">
          <groundspeak:date>2026-07-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP693 George Fox Trail [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s become a bit of a jungle here that requires careful stepping (and doesn’t make for a very dramatic cap picture) but I was able to find this before the parking lot filled for the soccer game.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="685177245">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2582877">manjalou</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 693 George Fox Trail&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were out caching in Cochrane  and stopped for a couple of BCPs as well. We parked in a sports field parking lot. Mr. ManjaLou was walking over in search of the BCP when a female RCMP officer stopped her car and asked him if he was having troubles. Mr. ManjaLou replied that &quot;No.. All was good and that he was just looking for the survey maker to take a picture&quot; . She replied &quot; oh yes.. They are starting construction here soon. Go right ahead&quot; and she drove off. Mr. ManjLou carried on to the cap and got his pictures. After relating his story to Mrs. ManjaLou we assumed she thought he was a worker. We found out later that they are replacing the hydro lines in this area. 

Thankyou for the cap Outforthehunt! (FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684621673">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6304346">sapien</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP693 George Fox Trail

N 51° 10.928 W 114° 29.403&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With all the markers at GZ, it appear there may be construction here very soon.  Hopefully this cap survives.  I was glad to see that someone before me had done all the heavy lifting finding this cap and I got to ride on their coat tails.  Koodos to them and TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684223575">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP693 - George Fox Trail&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, picking up ones we didn't get to earlier! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A busy day today and lots of walking, but a lot of fun!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; I know I've been here before... I think it was only for a traditional nearby though.  Convenient parking! No one playing nearby today either, so great timing for us!!  TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683871863">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP693 - George Fox Trail - a quick and easy find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
